WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.307
This module is really about meaning.

00:00:02.307 --> 00:00:08.632
Two columns can both be stored as integers and still require completely different analytical treatment.

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:11.887
A ZIP code uses digits but is a label.

00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:17.842
A satisfaction score may use one through five but represents ordered categories.

00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:20.267
A visit count is a true count.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:26.247
Celsius temperature is a measurement with equal differences but without a meaningful true zero.

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:31.817
That is why we do not let the software dtype make the analytical decision for us.

00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:35.597
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:40.122
an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:40.122 --> 00:00:46.562
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:46.562 --> 00:00:49.867
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:56.192
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:56.192 --> 00:00:59.537
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:59.537 --> 00:01:03.392
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
